From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 22:31:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] kernel 6.8: drop the gpio_cansleep branch in toggle_gpio

Kernel 6.8 removed gpio_cansleep from the legacy linux/gpio.h API, which is a
hard error (-Werror=implicit-function-declaration). Both branches did the same
thing apart from the cansleep variant of the set. The reset and boot lines are
on the PCA6408 expander on the camera i2c bus, so driving them sleeps, and
every caller runs in process context.
---
 ar0234.c | 12 +++++-------
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ar0234.c b/ar0234.c
index 31c244a..fe4bc58 100644
--- a/ar0234.c
+++ b/ar0234.c
@@ -711,13 +711,11 @@ int mcu_bload_ascii2hex(unsigned char ascii)
 
 static void toggle_gpio(unsigned int gpio, int val)
 {
-	if (gpio_cansleep(gpio)){
-		gpio_direction_output(gpio,val);
-		gpio_set_value_cansleep(gpio, val);
-	} else{
-		gpio_direction_output(gpio,val);
-		gpio_set_value(gpio, val);
-	}
+	/* The reset and boot lines hang off the PCA6408 expander on the camera's
+	 * i2c bus, so driving them sleeps. Every caller runs in process context.
+	 */
+	gpio_direction_output(gpio, val);
+	gpio_set_value_cansleep(gpio, val);
 }
 
 unsigned char errorcheck(char *data, unsigned int len)
